// args:
//   args.skip     = { tests: 'push/vg-e1r-tests', build: 'push/vg-e1r' }   steps already pushed ok (resume rule: nothing landed re-runs).
//   args.rulings  = 'push/vg-e1r-rulings'                                   merges an existing rulings branch into the builder and clerk.
//   args.specRef  = 'origin/main' (default)                                  where the spec is read from; the Preflight blocks if "Lane E1 part e" is absent there.
//   args.pieces   = comma-joined piece ids for pre-gate and gate, ONE third argument (default 'VG-E1R'); the Preflight names extra ids when a landing-record file (story_reviews/E.md, shots, the programme file, pieces.toml) has an owner the VG-E1R row lacks; the Dispatcher then relaunches with 'VG-E1R,<ids>' (pre_gate.sh forwards the string verbatim; footprint and size split on commas, acceptance and undertest look the whole string up as one id and WARN: the clerk lists those lines and runs the acceptance file itself).
//   args.pushMain = true by default (clean-gate push authorised by Westley's standing word); false for a branch-only landing.
//   args.files    = OPTIONAL extra source files the builder may edit (default none beyond the VG-E1R owns list); only with a ruling that adds them (gap 2 symbol row, gap 7 qa verb), each with an owner row.
//   args.gaps     = { hold, sigrows, full, tail, lotat, ring, play }   the Architect's ruling text for each numbered gap below. A key that is missing or empty stops the Preflight before any agent is spawned. Meaning of the values: hold = the release of the Architect's HOLD on csrc/economy_place.c (quote it); sigrows = the ruling on gap 2 (the Architect states which of its candidates holds and what rows/files follow); full = 'before' or 'after' (gap 3) or a ruling text; tail = 'zero' or 'keep' (gap 4) or text; lotat = the accepted observable proxy text (gap 5); ring = the fixture rule or amendment text (gap 6); play = 'defer' (sim-only landing, S-168 play untouched, the shot is not taken) or 'verb' (a place verb for the QA driver exists or is built; also pass args.placeVerb and args.files).
//   args.placeVerb = text, only with gaps.play 'verb': the exact QA-driver call the play uses to send a place command at a world point, and the owner row of the file that defines it.
//   args.baseRef  = '' (default)  STACKED BUILD (Architect 2026-10-14, rules.md (b) record pending; Westley: 'Claude compute used consistently'): comma list of the unlanded predecessor's pushed branches, in merge order, with or without origin/. E1r stacks on E7: baseRef 'push/vg-e7-land' (the E7 clerk's branch; it carries E7 and, through push/vg-e7-base, W2). Empty: every base is on origin/main and nothing below changes. Spec text is still read at args.specRef (origin/main). With a baseRef: (1) the Preflight scout merges the refs into its own scratch tree and checks every TREE precondition there (the chain: ABI 8, save format 12, the two-argument starting-force functions, tests/csim/test_VG_E_e7.py present; the sig-rows, owner rows and baselines), not on bare origin/main; the VG-W2 and VG-CONTRACT-E7 rows need not be attached; it reports whether each ref is already an ancestor of origin/main; (2) a Base phase builds and pushes push/vg-e1r-base = origin/main + each baseRef (a conflict in code or tests stops: stop_reason base-conflict), and every later worktree, pre-gate, Check and comparison uses it in place of origin/main; (3) the clerk pushes main ONLY if every baseRef is already an ancestor of origin/main; otherwise it stops at push/vg-e1r-land with everything done except the gate, the landing edits and the push (stop_reason 'stacked-waits-for-bases'; the landing queue keeps the order, the predecessor first); (4) when the predecessor has landed, relaunch with baseRef '' and args.skip for every finished step: the Check then re-runs against origin/main with the landed predecessor merged in (if the predecessor changed in its own gate this is the rework check, no re-draft), and the clerk merges origin/main, re-runs the tests and gates. Example: Workflow({scriptPath, args: {baseRef: 'push/vg-e7-land', gaps: {...}}}). args.skip may also carry base: 'push/vg-e1r-base' (a Base step already pushed ok).
